      "text": "Let's start by letting \\( y = \\frac{4x-16}{3x-4} \\). The given equation is:\n\n\\[\ny^2 + y = 12\n\\]\n\nThis is a quadratic equation in terms of \\( y \\). To solve for \\( y \\), we rearrange the equation as follows:\n\n\\[\ny^2 + y - 12 = 0\n\\]\n\nWe can factor this quadratic equation:\n\n\\[\n(y + 4)(y - 3) = 0\n\\]\n\nSetting each factor equal to zero gives us the solutions:\n\n\\[\ny + 4 = 0 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad y - 3 = 0\n\\]\n\n\\[\ny = -4 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad y = 3\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to find the corresponding values of \\( x \\) for each value of \\( y \\).\n\n1. For \\( y = -4 \\):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{4x-16}{3x-4} = -4\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\( x \\):\n\n\\[\n4x - 16 = -4(3x - 4)\n\\]\n\n\\[\n4x - 16 = -12x + 16\n\\]\n\n\\[\n4x + 12x = 16 + 16\n\\]\n\n\\[\n16x = 32\n\\]\n\n\\[\nx = 2\n\\]\n\n2. For \\( y = 3 \\):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{4x-16}{3x-4} = 3\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\( x \\):\n\n\\[\n4x - 16 = 3(3x - 4)\n\\]\n\n\\[\n4x - 16 = 9x - 12\n\\]\n\n\\[\n4x - 9x = -12 + 16\n\\]\n\n\\[\n-5x = 4\n\\]\n\n\\[\nx = -\\frac{4}{5}\n\\]\n\nThe greatest possible value of \\( x \\) is \\(-\\frac{4}{5}\\).\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{-\\frac{4}{5}}\n\\]",
