      "text": "To solve the equation \\(\\left(\\frac{4x-16}{3x-4}\\right)^2 + \\left(\\frac{4x-16}{3x-4}\\right) = 12\\), let's follow these steps:\n\n1. Let \\( y = \\frac{4x-16}{3x-4} \\). The equation then becomes:\n   \\[\n   y^2 + y = 12\n   \\]\n2. Rearrange this to form a standard quadratic equation:\n   \\[\n   y^2 + y - 12 = 0\n   \\]\n3. Factor the quadratic equation:\n   \\[\n   (y - 3)(y + 4) = 0\n   \\]\n   So, the solutions for \\( y \\) are:\n   \\[\n   y = 3 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad y = -4\n   \\]\n4. Recall that \\( y = \\frac{4x-16}{3x-4} \\). We need to solve for \\( x \\) in each case.\n\n**Case 1: \\( y = 3 \\)**\n\\[\n3 = \\frac{4x-16}{3x-4}\n\\]\nMultiply both sides by \\( 3x-4 \\):\n\\[\n3(3x-4) = 4x-16\n\\]\n\\[\n9x - 12 = 4x - 16\n\\]\n\\[\n9x - 4x = -16 + 12\n\\]\n\\[\n5x = -4\n\\]\n\\[\nx = -\\frac{4}{5}\n\\]\n\n**Case 2: \\( y = -4 \\)**\n\\[\n-4 = \\frac{4x-16}{3x-4}\n\\]\nMultiply both sides by \\( 3x-4 \\):\n\\[\n-4(3x-4) = 4x-16\n\\]\n\\[\n-12x + 16 = 4x - 16\n\\]\n\\[\n-12x - 4x = -16 - 16\n\\]\n\\[\n-16x = -32\n\\]\n\\[\nx = 2\n\\]\n\nThe greatest possible value of \\( x \\) is therefore \\( 2 \\).\n\nThe final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{2}\n\\]",
